        "category": "client/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/client/GcsReadChannelMetadataExtractor.java:165",
        "finding": "The cache population method `addMatchingZeroArgMethods` calls `method.setAccessible(true)` without catching `RuntimeException`. On Java 9+, `setAccessible(true)` can throw `InaccessibleObjectException` for public methods of classes in closed modules. In the original code, this was safely caught by `invokeLongGetter`'s `try...catch (ReflectiveOperationException | RuntimeException e)`, allowing graceful fallback to the next getter or returning `-1L`. In this new code, an inaccessible getter will crash `ClassValue.computeValue` and fail the entire `extract()` method. You must catch and ignore `RuntimeException` around `setAccessible` here, just like you did in `ChannelAccessors.forClass`.",
        "source": "critic_history"
      }
